  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5102.801 Spofford Lake",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5102.801 Spofford Lake. The portion of Spofford Lake between route 63 and Eel Rock in the town of Chesterfield, and more specifically described as the area bordered by the northwesterly black topped buoy marking Eel Rock reef, then westerly to shoreline of Route 63, and travel southerly along Route 63 and then back easterly to the southerly most marked red topped buoy marking Eel Rock, shall be a “no wake” area.\n\nSource. #11100, EXEMPT, eff 5-19-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5100.html"
}
